WEBVTT

01:47.160 --> 01:51.540
The Witch's Pastime:
Final Act

01:52.180 --> 01:56.720
We suspect a witch, based on 
the overwhelming power.

01:56.720 --> 01:59.590
Then there are the messages
left at the crime scenes.

01:59.980 --> 02:03.220
Each one points to the killer being a witch.

02:03.220 --> 02:05.200
Oh? For example?

02:05.200 --> 02:09.650
"I live on and on without change. 
I bear heir after heir without change."

02:09.650 --> 02:11.310
Do you know what that points to?

02:11.310 --> 02:15.080
A witch. Witches don't age 
and their health doesn't decline.

02:15.080 --> 02:18.150
And a witch's power is 
passed on to her descendants,

02:18.150 --> 02:20.450
so even having children doesn't change th—

02:21.300 --> 02:22.400
What is it?

02:22.400 --> 02:25.200
The killer wants to declare 
that they are a witch.

02:25.200 --> 02:26.950
I bet all the answers are "witch."

02:27.220 --> 02:28.760
What about this one?

02:28.760 --> 02:32.750
"Four legs in the morning, 
two legs at noon, three legs at night."

02:32.750 --> 02:33.710
A witch.

02:33.930 --> 02:35.560
A human, I believe.

02:35.560 --> 02:36.870
Right. A human.

02:37.560 --> 02:40.500
How strange. Was that one of the messages?

02:40.500 --> 02:43.760
That's right. None of it 
means much of anything.

02:43.760 --> 02:45.970
The killer's laughing at us.

02:45.970 --> 02:51.740
We call it the "Witch's Pastime" case
because it's all a game to them.

02:56.360 --> 02:58.450
But that game has come back to bite them.

02:58.450 --> 03:03.910
I realized that some of the riddles 
were quotes from a book.

03:04.520 --> 03:07.890
And it seems this bookshop
had ordered a copy of it.

03:07.890 --> 03:09.870
Even the timing lines up.

03:10.130 --> 03:12.580
I'm impressed you traced the quotations.

03:12.580 --> 03:16.500
I just got lucky. 
I have the same book at home.

03:19.220 --> 03:20.320
Something stinks.

03:24.680 --> 03:26.010
What do you think you're doing?!

03:27.200 --> 03:28.840
You guys go in.

03:41.600 --> 03:42.860
Damn it!

03:45.200 --> 03:47.910
The wound shows magical damage.

03:47.910 --> 03:51.120
It seems natural to conclude 
that a witch inflicted it.

03:51.120 --> 03:54.770
She must have gouged out his eyes
 because he saw something.

03:54.770 --> 03:56.750
An attempt at irony, I assume.

03:57.260 --> 03:59.460
If she intended to cover her trail this way,

03:59.460 --> 04:02.720
why bother leaving quotations 
as messages in the first place?

04:03.150 --> 04:07.020
I told you. It's just a game to her.

04:07.020 --> 04:10.930
She probably just decided 
she might as well kill this guy, too.

04:10.930 --> 04:13.030
We've lost our lead.

04:13.030 --> 04:16.650
You look exhausted. 
Perhaps you could use some rest?

04:17.330 --> 04:19.890
You shouldn't get too close to me.

04:20.260 --> 04:21.220
Why not?

04:21.880 --> 04:23.350
Because of precedent.

04:24.440 --> 04:27.340
Nothing good happens to people I'm close to.

04:30.860 --> 04:31.910
What is it?

04:31.910 --> 04:35.370
Ms. Haines, we've found a new body here, too.

04:35.890 --> 04:37.530
<i>And a message.</i>

04:37.530 --> 04:38.840
What's it say?

04:41.440 --> 04:43.420
<i>I'm a disease.</i>

04:43.420 --> 04:46.630
<i>Diseases propagate and spread.</i>

04:46.630 --> 04:50.710
<i>This disease is called a curse.
 A witch's curse.</i>

04:53.170 --> 04:57.480
Considering I took you to the crime scene,
 you didn't manage to find out much.

04:57.730 --> 05:01.080
Oh, well. Corpses aren't my specialty.

05:01.080 --> 05:03.490
Well, I'm not expecting much, anyway.

05:03.990 --> 05:04.700
See you.

05:09.220 --> 05:10.240
Ashaf.

05:10.990 --> 05:12.240
Yes?

05:12.240 --> 05:14.710
Get ready. Something's here.

05:14.710 --> 05:16.540
Really? You must be joking.

05:17.000 --> 05:19.120
I left the coffin at the hotel.

05:21.690 --> 05:23.800
Idiot! Don't just rush in blindly!

05:37.820 --> 05:39.150
She disappeared!

05:39.380 --> 05:43.180
That she did. Quite literally like smoke.

05:43.180 --> 05:45.920
So she's powerful and an escape artist, too?

05:45.920 --> 05:47.860
I'd say we have our work cut out for us.

05:48.350 --> 05:50.360
Still, why would the witch...

05:50.360 --> 05:51.830
She was tailing her.

05:52.200 --> 05:53.080
What?

05:53.320 --> 05:57.120
Ever since we met up with that woman, 
I've felt someone watching us.

05:57.120 --> 05:59.290
Looks like I wasn't imagining it.

05:59.290 --> 06:00.110
Shit!

06:06.170 --> 06:08.260
I'd like to ask you something.

06:09.720 --> 06:11.470
What happened to you?

06:11.470 --> 06:13.470
We had a little run-in with the witch.

06:13.470 --> 06:14.560
And you lost her?

06:14.560 --> 06:16.430
Yes, completely.

06:16.430 --> 06:17.420
I see.

06:17.770 --> 06:20.150
There goes what little hope I had for you.

06:20.850 --> 06:22.980
You took quite a beating.

06:22.980 --> 06:25.190
I've already performed healing.

06:25.190 --> 06:27.620
More importantly, 
please answer my question.

06:28.610 --> 06:31.170
How are you connected to the witch?

06:31.170 --> 06:32.160
What?

06:32.590 --> 06:34.950
It seems you were followed.

06:35.200 --> 06:37.690
The witch must know what you look like,

06:37.690 --> 06:42.560
so we can safely assume 
she tailed you, not us.

06:42.560 --> 06:45.850
Why does the witch make a point
 of announcing what she is?

06:45.850 --> 06:48.170
Presumably to mobilize the Paladins.

06:48.170 --> 06:50.400
Who likes fighting small fry?

06:50.400 --> 06:53.930
But no matter how long she waits, 
only the police oppose her.

06:53.930 --> 06:56.890
So to draw out the Paladins...

06:57.220 --> 06:59.600
Guideau, what would you do?

07:00.000 --> 07:02.220
Kill all the small fry.

07:02.220 --> 07:02.940
Or...

07:03.280 --> 07:05.630
take out their boss.

07:07.350 --> 07:10.810
The mayor's egotism caused this situation.

07:10.810 --> 07:13.340
But only insiders know that.

07:13.340 --> 07:18.810
Most would assume the police would be 
lost without you, their only real fighter.

07:19.230 --> 07:22.500
And yet, despite all of that 
as well as shadowing you,

07:22.500 --> 07:26.340
the witch waited until we split up, 
and then targeted <i>us</i>.

07:26.860 --> 07:28.320
Why?

07:28.320 --> 07:30.220
Why won't she go after me?!

07:30.560 --> 07:32.810
Why follow me if she 
doesn't want to kill me?!

07:33.280 --> 07:36.180
I don't know. That's why I asked.

07:36.390 --> 07:37.740
Don't tell me...

07:37.740 --> 07:39.480
Could it be...

07:39.480 --> 07:43.150
So you <i>do</i> know something. Cough it up!

07:44.610 --> 07:48.780
This case, needless to say, had a beginning.

07:50.290 --> 07:52.240
I don't often see you this early, Kiera.

07:52.550 --> 07:55.340
I always run late. If I don't go home early

07:55.340 --> 07:59.040
and eat with the kids when I can,
what kind of mother am I?

08:00.480 --> 08:01.750
Ms. Haines!

08:02.340 --> 08:03.210
What is it?

08:04.500 --> 08:06.300
Your house just...

08:09.590 --> 08:11.670
Ms. Haines, it's dangerous!

08:11.670 --> 08:13.630
My children are in there!

08:14.050 --> 08:16.350
Shulk! Loran!

08:22.170 --> 08:23.960
Were there any witnesses?

08:23.960 --> 08:26.440
Local residents have given us information.

08:26.760 --> 08:30.900
And we think the culprit left a 
message on a wall across the street.

08:33.700 --> 08:38.580
"I live on and on without change. 
I bear heir after heir without change."

08:38.860 --> 08:40.770
What could it mean?

08:41.180 --> 08:42.230
A witch.

08:45.580 --> 08:47.810
It's the time that was on the warning note.

08:47.810 --> 08:48.620
Yeah.

08:51.320 --> 08:53.440
Damn it! Not this purple smoke again!

08:53.440 --> 08:55.000
We can't get a clear view!

08:55.000 --> 08:57.390
Everyone, take shelter 
in the magical array!

08:57.800 --> 08:59.010
What are you doing, Reuben?!

08:59.010 --> 09:00.300
I'll take her down.

09:00.300 --> 09:02.700
Alone? That's crazy! She's a witch!

09:02.700 --> 09:07.020
Yes, I know. The witch who killed those kids!

09:20.300 --> 09:23.250
I lost my sons and Reuben.

09:24.180 --> 09:28.300
He was my magic teacher... and my boyfriend.

09:31.840 --> 09:34.320
I suspect that warning was meant to...

09:34.320 --> 09:36.920
What you told me clinches it.

09:37.600 --> 09:40.120
It was to lure him out and murder him.

09:40.780 --> 09:43.510
The witch is targeting people I care about.

09:44.320 --> 09:46.690
You got too friendly with me.

09:46.690 --> 09:49.050
So we gave her the wrong idea, huh?

09:49.050 --> 09:51.120
But that clarifies things.

09:51.120 --> 09:53.650
The witch must hold a grudge against you.

09:53.650 --> 09:54.910
Any idea why?

09:54.910 --> 09:56.490
Of course not.

09:56.490 --> 09:57.810
But that's perfect.

09:58.260 --> 10:02.950
If she's hung up on me, 
I may get a shot at revenge.

10:03.220 --> 10:05.060
Revenge, huh?

10:05.060 --> 10:08.960
I see. So that's why you went 
along with the mayor's lies.

10:09.640 --> 10:10.960
Do you blame me?

10:11.910 --> 10:15.930
I put my revenge ahead 
of the lives of citizens,

10:15.930 --> 10:18.430
and keep racking up needless sacrifices.

10:18.830 --> 10:22.440
I don't have the sense of duty 
and justice a detective should.

10:22.870 --> 10:25.890
I won't fault you, but are you certain?

10:26.220 --> 10:27.770
You look miserable.

10:27.770 --> 10:29.440
Don't talk like you understand.

10:30.000 --> 10:33.540
Even if you do get your revenge, 
who will celebrate it?

10:33.540 --> 10:34.860
I know!

10:35.190 --> 10:39.620
I know I'm not strong enough, 
and that no one wants revenge.

10:39.620 --> 10:41.870
I don't need you to tell me that!

10:41.870 --> 10:47.700
But I still can't do anything 
about this pain... this hatred.

10:49.200 --> 10:50.670
What the hell?

10:50.670 --> 10:53.520
You keep spouting crap that makes no sense.

10:53.520 --> 10:56.250
If you wanna get even, you do it.

10:56.960 --> 10:58.970
Who gives a shit who you do it for?

10:59.250 --> 11:01.010
You said it yourself.

11:01.010 --> 11:02.740
You'll kill her 'cause you hate her.

11:02.740 --> 11:04.810
You'll kill her 'cause you want relief.

11:05.020 --> 11:07.230
Revenge feels great.

11:08.270 --> 11:10.040
Wh-What do you...

11:10.040 --> 11:11.370
I'm not like you!

11:11.370 --> 11:13.190
Why would you encourage her?

11:13.190 --> 11:14.280
Ms. Haines!

11:15.000 --> 11:16.530
The witch has sent a warning!

11:16.530 --> 11:18.990
She's coming to the station in three days!

11:19.410 --> 11:23.530
Goodness. She must want to 
kill someone there at any cost.

11:23.530 --> 11:25.010
Can I trust you?

11:25.860 --> 11:29.790
Can I really trust you to 
measure up to the witch?

11:29.790 --> 11:31.300
Damn right you can.

11:32.760 --> 11:34.210
I'll teach you...

11:34.800 --> 11:37.900
what makes revenge so sweet.

11:44.970 --> 11:48.930
The witch's main spell is purple smoke.
 I don't know how it works.

11:49.480 --> 11:53.200
She can crush most things with it,
 or send them flying.

11:53.200 --> 11:55.020
It also acts as a smoke screen.

11:55.970 --> 11:59.250
I suppose her vanishing spell 
is our biggest concern.

12:00.380 --> 12:04.210
By the way, what did you do 
with those leather sacks I got you?

12:04.210 --> 12:05.700
Oh, nothing much.

12:07.770 --> 12:10.790
About Guideau... I know what she said,

12:11.330 --> 12:16.210
but if we manage to beat this witch, 
will that cheer everyone up a little?

12:16.890 --> 12:18.780
Yes, I'm sure it will.

12:19.670 --> 12:21.120
She's late.

12:21.120 --> 12:23.310
I've already digested everything I ate.

12:23.310 --> 12:25.640
Give us a time of day, too, asshole.

12:26.030 --> 12:27.600
How are you feeling?

12:27.600 --> 12:28.830
Huh?!

12:28.830 --> 12:30.670
What are you, some street thug?

12:31.350 --> 12:35.470
Anyway, how on earth do 
you plan to fight the witch?

12:35.470 --> 12:37.000
Shut up and watch.

12:37.000 --> 12:40.000
Once I undo the curse on me, 
this witch will be a pushover.

12:40.000 --> 12:40.980
Wait a minute!

12:41.390 --> 12:43.750
Don't tell me you're counting on <i>that</i>?

12:43.750 --> 12:46.630
You must know how to undo a witch's curse.

12:46.630 --> 12:51.670
You either kiss your true love, or get the 
witch who cast the curse to undo it. That's it!

12:51.670 --> 12:54.980
Can you prove this witch 
is the one who cursed you?

12:54.980 --> 12:56.500
'Course not.

12:56.500 --> 12:57.820
Don't worry.

12:58.500 --> 13:02.500
You see, there's actually one 
more way to undo the curse.

13:03.310 --> 13:06.000
That's what we're gambling on.

13:06.000 --> 13:09.890
If we face a witch and meet certain 
conditions, we'll see the return

13:10.220 --> 13:12.650
of a monster even witches fear.

13:14.860 --> 13:16.230
She's here.

13:19.830 --> 13:20.940
I see her.

13:21.270 --> 13:22.070
Get ready!

13:22.670 --> 13:24.300
Don't jump the gun, Guideau.

13:24.300 --> 13:25.110
Huh?

13:32.520 --> 13:35.330
Good grief. Rampaging right out of the gate.

13:37.340 --> 13:38.640
What's that sound?

13:38.640 --> 13:41.130
Watch out! She's up to her old tricks!

13:42.410 --> 13:44.100
What just happened?!

13:44.100 --> 13:48.110
<i>Given how little we can see, we can't 
attack recklessly because we have allies.</i>

13:48.110 --> 13:50.480
<i>But our opponent is free to cut loose.</i>

13:52.610 --> 13:54.350
<i>Hardly an enviable position.</i>

14:07.880 --> 14:09.280
Are you all unharmed?

14:09.280 --> 14:13.850
Yeah. I can manage as long as 
I focus solely on staying alive.

14:15.250 --> 14:16.130
Guideau!

14:17.350 --> 14:18.460
That asshole!

14:18.460 --> 14:22.940
Thank goodness. That means 
we kept our losses to a minimum.

14:22.940 --> 14:26.590
This sucks. Just let me kill her ass already!

14:26.840 --> 14:30.390
What good will fighting do when 
our enemy has a way to escape?

14:30.390 --> 14:32.890
We should corner her before we strike.

14:32.890 --> 14:35.320
I've done everything you've said so far.

14:35.320 --> 14:37.850
You'd better have a plan for what comes next.

14:37.850 --> 14:40.590
Not a problem. I've already found her.

14:41.340 --> 14:42.770
How on earth...

14:43.600 --> 14:46.230
Have you noticed that 
there are more crows lately?

14:48.670 --> 14:50.950
Those are my familiars.

14:51.270 --> 14:56.750
And I can see everything they can.

14:57.390 --> 15:00.000
So she can't escape us now, 
no matter where she goes.

15:00.770 --> 15:04.550
Now, shall we go see a witch?

15:31.110 --> 15:31.820
Huh?!

15:35.130 --> 15:38.410
Honestly. Must you charge
in alone every single time?

15:38.880 --> 15:41.370
Ashaf, there were two of 'em.

15:41.670 --> 15:45.130
No, forget that. Damn it!

15:45.130 --> 15:48.280
These assholes aren't witches!

15:48.530 --> 15:52.020
Tch, another one. How'd they find us?

15:52.760 --> 15:54.470
Dude, you survived?!

15:54.470 --> 15:57.180
Yes. Did you think you'd killed me?

15:57.180 --> 16:00.500
Well, of course you would,
after a rampage like that.

16:00.500 --> 16:03.170
Unfortunately for you, 
I have confidence in my wards.

16:03.170 --> 16:06.090
Damn. This guy's a mage.

16:06.090 --> 16:07.610
Are you two alone?

16:11.710 --> 16:15.010
What's going on here? It can't be...

16:15.010 --> 16:18.580
You're alive, Shulk? Loran?

16:20.020 --> 16:22.010
Ah, crap.

16:22.010 --> 16:24.890
You're the last person we wanted to find out.

16:25.610 --> 16:26.910
You know them?

16:27.740 --> 16:31.880
They're my sons. 
The ones I told you the witch killed.

16:32.400 --> 16:33.590
But how?

16:34.210 --> 16:35.740
What are you doing here?

16:37.050 --> 16:38.200
Don't tell me...

16:39.520 --> 16:40.770
There's no way!

16:41.190 --> 16:41.980
Loran...

16:41.980 --> 16:43.180
Shulk...

16:43.960 --> 16:46.270
<i>You</i> were the witch?

16:46.270 --> 16:48.560
No, that can't be.

16:48.560 --> 16:51.440
I know you don't have that kind of power.

16:51.670 --> 16:54.250
Look at what they're holding, Kiera.

16:55.520 --> 16:58.320
There's the truth behind 
their witch-like power.

16:59.090 --> 17:02.540
The two-volume grimoire, Sarnovasus.

17:02.540 --> 17:04.000
A grimoire?

17:04.430 --> 17:08.190
Grimoires provide power and 
perform spells for their wielders.

17:08.190 --> 17:10.860
No magical aptitude is needed.

17:10.860 --> 17:13.940
Just holding one grants power 
almost on par with a witch's.

17:13.940 --> 17:17.720
They're a type of Forbidden Instrument, 
which are taboo tools of dark magic.

17:17.720 --> 17:21.460
And either part of a two-volume grimoire

17:21.460 --> 17:24.680
can summon its other half 
instantly across space.

17:24.680 --> 17:28.150
But only up to a distance 
of roughly one kilometer.

17:28.530 --> 17:31.070
So I was able to locate them
 in next to no time.

17:31.070 --> 17:32.860
Who is this guy?

17:32.860 --> 17:36.170
Where did you get something like that?

17:36.170 --> 17:38.910
What are you talking about? 
They were on your desk!

17:38.910 --> 17:39.820
What?

17:40.100 --> 17:42.660
You have no right to punish us!

17:42.910 --> 17:45.620
It's your fault we ended up this way!

17:45.910 --> 17:48.300
We don't kill because we like it!

17:48.300 --> 17:52.340
These grimoires give us power, 
but we have to feed them lives!

17:52.340 --> 17:55.470
They'll eat <i>us</i> if we don't 
give them sacrifices!

17:55.470 --> 17:57.590
Touching the grimoires made us this way!

17:57.590 --> 17:59.860
So we <i>had</i> to kill!

17:59.860 --> 18:01.250
No...

18:03.690 --> 18:05.570
That's a good one.

18:05.570 --> 18:08.480
I've seen the bodies of a few people you killed,

18:08.790 --> 18:11.940
and I could tell you loved every moment.

18:12.370 --> 18:16.200
You had to? You had no choice?

18:16.720 --> 18:18.150
Then...

18:18.150 --> 18:21.010
Then why did you kill Reuben?!

18:21.010 --> 18:23.370
He loved you both, too!

18:25.130 --> 18:26.460
That's enough.

18:26.930 --> 18:29.940
We don't owe you all the answers.

18:30.420 --> 18:32.960
And this is a fight to the death!

18:36.050 --> 18:37.300
Unfortunately for you,

18:37.630 --> 18:41.680
there are three reasons why 
you stand no chance against us.

18:41.680 --> 18:42.850
Huh?

18:42.850 --> 18:47.310
First, you failed to pay 
your grimoires' price.

18:47.650 --> 18:49.040
What are you talking about?!

18:49.040 --> 18:52.040
I know we killed at least ten people today!

18:52.040 --> 18:53.210
We made our sacrifices!

18:53.210 --> 18:55.590
Oh, you mean these?

18:59.690 --> 19:00.820
What the hell is that?!

19:01.200 --> 19:05.440
A mere dummy. A leather sack 
stuffed full of red liquid.

19:05.440 --> 19:08.140
Well, they don't stand up
 to close inspection,

19:08.140 --> 19:11.250
but your smoke made it awfully hard to see.

19:11.250 --> 19:12.800
So what?!

19:12.800 --> 19:16.350
With this power, we can kill all we need!

19:16.920 --> 19:18.090
I'll crush you!

19:26.610 --> 19:29.810
Second, even without undoing the curse...

19:32.300 --> 19:34.440
we're fairly strong.

19:37.530 --> 19:40.400
Well, what do you know? 
We didn't need number three.

19:40.400 --> 19:43.890
You punks don't have what it takes
 to call yourselves witches.

19:43.890 --> 19:45.180
Assholes.

19:48.390 --> 19:50.580
Why did you pretend to be witches?

19:51.200 --> 19:54.540
So we wouldn't have to fight you.

19:54.900 --> 19:59.120
You were too young to be our mother.

19:59.120 --> 20:02.010
We could only see you as a woman.

20:02.340 --> 20:05.880
We couldn't let anyone get near you, Kiera.

20:06.820 --> 20:08.300
We love you!

20:08.300 --> 20:10.810
You love us, too! Don't you, Kiera?!

20:11.440 --> 20:14.140
If you won't end this, 
get outta my way and I'll do it.

20:15.000 --> 20:16.200
I'm fine.

20:18.260 --> 20:19.780
I'll do it.

20:19.780 --> 20:21.330
W-Wait!

20:21.330 --> 20:23.360
Why?! You'd just abandon us?!

20:23.600 --> 20:26.120
You said you loved us!

20:26.410 --> 20:27.780
I did love you.

20:28.550 --> 20:30.210
But you crossed a line.

20:31.020 --> 20:33.440
Now I don't even pity you.

20:37.900 --> 20:40.340
Why'd you adopt us?

20:41.700 --> 20:43.630
Because I wanted you to know.

20:43.630 --> 20:44.630
Know what?

20:43.630 --> 20:44.630
Know what?

20:44.980 --> 20:46.900
What it is to love and be loved.

20:47.630 --> 20:49.660
Ordinary things like that.

20:53.610 --> 20:57.640
<i>The Witch's Pastime case,
which has long tormented Hayden,</i>

20:57.640 --> 20:59.900
<i>was thought to be the work of a witch,</i>

20:59.900 --> 21:04.200
<i>but we have just learned that 
two boys committed the killings.</i>

21:04.430 --> 21:08.660
Damn it, Ashaf. You knew the 
witch was a fake, didn't you?

21:08.950 --> 21:13.040
Well, you catch on quick when you know
 as many dark secrets as the Order does.

21:13.040 --> 21:17.540
Nothing would have kept the 
Paladin Corps out of a real witch case.

21:17.800 --> 21:19.450
You'll pay once I'm done eating.

21:19.450 --> 21:21.620
Now, now. Be reasonable.

21:22.470 --> 21:23.510
Hey.

21:23.950 --> 21:24.790
Kiera.

21:26.170 --> 21:27.530
Thanks.

21:27.530 --> 21:30.820
We really wouldn't have had 
a prayer without you two.

21:30.820 --> 21:31.930
Just doing our job.

21:32.430 --> 21:35.140
And we'll be taking the grimoires with us.

21:35.810 --> 21:37.050
The grimoires...

21:37.050 --> 21:40.030
I don't remember ever seeing them before.

21:40.030 --> 21:42.140
Forbidden Instruments 
have wills of their own.

21:42.140 --> 21:44.740
They find the right person at the right time.

21:45.040 --> 21:47.630
You mean they got there on their own?

21:47.630 --> 21:50.170
That may just be what happened.

21:50.960 --> 21:53.580
They were never the best behaved of boys,

21:53.580 --> 21:58.300
but they never would have turned out 
that way if not for those grimoires.

21:59.330 --> 22:02.590
The deaths they would have 
suffered for failing to pay the price

22:02.590 --> 22:05.140
would likely have been far more horrible.

22:09.540 --> 22:10.730
I'll be going now.

22:12.020 --> 22:12.860
Kiera.

22:14.550 --> 22:18.270
Next time you run into trouble, drop us a line.

22:21.680 --> 22:22.860
Sure.

22:23.810 --> 22:25.110
I'll give you a call.

22:25.580 --> 22:29.140
If a witch shows up, you can count on it.

24:00.450 --> 24:06.460
Naturally, we retain a 
necromantic specialist.

24:06.460 --> 24:10.710
Beauty and Death

24:06.460 --> 24:10.710
Opening Act

24:06.710 --> 24:09.880
Next time: "Beauty and Death: Opening Act."
